` A DCC throttle on Leah's own base station board, checked by a second board: the safe ladder's step 2
` (design/model_railroading.md, "Stage 1b"). No motor shield, no track, no locomotive: the base station
` (an Arduino Mega) makes the real DCC signal as 5 V logic on its pin 12, and the reader (an Arduino Uno
` or Nano, its pin 8 joined to the Mega's pin 12 through a 1 kOhm resistor, the grounds joined) reads it
` back as a decoder would, and tells Leah what it heard and how long each half-bit lasted.
`
` Choose the two boards' ports, load Leah's programs onto them once, connect, and drive.

$base = null
$loco = null
$shown = ""
` (The programs being loaded, kept so their on_finished still runs.)
$loading = []

$win = window(title: "DCC bench", width: 860, height: 600, minimum_width: 780, minimum_height: 560)

` -- the boards --
$boards_box = group_box(left: 20, top: 16, width: 820, height: 170, text: "The boards", lock_right: true)
